---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const updated = '19 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Terms of use | Fog Off" description="What Fog Off is, what it is not, and the rules for using and contributing.">
  <article class="wrap" style="padding-block:56px 0; max-width:800px;">
    <span class="pill">Terms of use</span>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem); letter-spacing:-0.03em; line-height:1.1; margin:16px 0;">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="draft"><strong>Draft, not yet reviewed by a legal adviser.</strong> Items shown as square brackets highlighted in yellow must be completed before launch. Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <h2>1. What Fog Off is</h2>
    <p>Fog Off is a free information service run by {SITE.operator ? <strong>{SITE.operator}</strong> : <span class="todo">[YOUR NAME OR COMPANY NAME]</span>} (contact: {SITE.email ? <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> : <span class="todo">[CONTACT EMAIL]</span>}). It helps you understand what can change a UK car insurance quote, and it shows general findings from tests.</p>

    <h2>2. What Fog Off is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Not an insurer, broker or adviser.</strong> We are not authorised or regulated by the Financial Conduct Authority. We do not sell, arrange or advise on insurance, we do not show live quotes, and we do not recommend any insurer, policy, comparison site or job title.</li>
      <li><strong>Not personal advice.</strong> Lists such as "what is worth testing" and labels such as "fit for your answers" are general information based on broad categories and limited data. They are not a recommendation to you. Prices, rules and results change often and may be different for you.</li>
      <li><strong>No commission.</strong> We are funded by donations. We have no affiliate links.</li>
      <li>We are not connected to any comparison site or insurer. Names belong to their owners.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Answer every insurance question <strong>truthfully and completely</strong> when you buy. A false or careless answer can reduce or void a claim payout and may have other legal effects.</li>
      <li>Tests are for learning how prices respond. Only try options that are genuinely true or genuinely possible for you (for example a driver who really would drive, or a job title that is accurate). Never buy a policy on details that are not true.</li>
      <li>Check each comparison site's and insurer's own terms before you run test quotes. You are responsible for how you use them.</li>
      <li>Check cover, limits, exclusions and the total cost with the insurer before you buy. A lower price can mean less cover.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Sharing a report</h2>
    <p>If you share a report you confirm that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the percentages come from your own genuine test quotes;</li>
      <li>nothing in it is personal data about anyone else; and</li>
      <li>you do not send false, automated or bulk reports.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You allow us to use the banded data to calculate and publish group figures, and to keep it for the period in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>. We may remove any report, or stop publishing any figure, that looks unreliable. We may limit how many reports are accepted to protect the service.</p>

    <h2>5. Accuracy and availability</h2>
    <p>We try to keep the information accurate and up to date, but we give no promise that it is complete, current or suitable for you. The service is provided "as is" and may change, pause or stop at any time.</p>

    <h2 id="made">6. How the site was made</h2>
    <p>Fog Off was designed and built with the help of AI tools, including the text, the code and the artwork. A person reviews and publishes it, but AI can make mistakes, so please check anything important. The figures in the findings come from tests and community reports, not from AI.</p>

    <h2>7. Liability</h2>
    <p>Nothing in these terms limits or excludes liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, or for anything else that cannot legally be limited. Subject to that, we are not liable for losses that result from relying on the information here, including a refused or reduced insurance claim, a higher premium, or choices you make after using the tools. If you use the service as a consumer, your legal rights are not affected.</p>

    <h2>8. Licences and use of the site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Code:</strong> PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (see the repository). Free for personal, research, educational and non-profit use. Commercial use needs permission.</li>
      <li><strong>Guide text and published findings:</strong> Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (credit "Fog Off").</li>
      <li><strong>Name and logo:</strong> all rights reserved.</li>
      <li>Do not scrape the site or the findings at a rate that harms it, send automated reports, or try to identify or contact other contributors.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Changes and law</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms. The date above shows the latest version. These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts there have jurisdiction, subject to any rights you have as a consumer where you live.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 34px 0 8px; }
  p, li { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .draft { background: var(--warn-soft); padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 12px; }
  a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
